## Build and Run

> Replace `mini_strace.c` with the actual name of your source file.

**Compile**

```bash
gcc -o mini_strace mini_strace.c
```

**Run**

```bash
./mini_strace <program> [arguments...]
```

**Example**

```bash
./mini_strace ls -l
```

## Sample Output (Illustrative)

> **Illustrative only.** The output below shows the kind of information the tool is meant to display. It has not been captured from a validated run. Actual output depends on the program being traced, the architecture, and your implementation.

```
$ ./mini_strace ./hello
syscall 59 entry
syscall 59 exit
syscall 1 entry
syscall 1 exit
syscall 231 entry
```

On x86-64 Linux, `59` is `execve`, `1` is `write`, and `231` is `exit_group`. System-call numbers differ between architectures.

